Azure Policy provides a mechanism for enforcing organizational standards and assessing compliance across Azure resources. Instead of relying entirely on administrators to manually verify configurations, policies can automatically evaluate resources against defined requirements.

Common policy scenarios include:

* Restricting allowed Azure regions
* Requiring resource tags
* Enforcing specific resource configurations
* Auditing unsupported resource types
* Enforcing security standards
* Maintaining organizational compliance

For example, an organization operating only in approved geographic locations can create a policy that prevents resources from being deployed outside those regions.

A real-life use case is a regulated enterprise ensuring that all production resources follow predefined security and governance requirements.

Azure Policy helps organizations maintain consistent governance at scale.
